       "Viruses were discovered by Ivanowski in 1892 and TMV was crystallised by Stanley; viroids (Diener) and prions are infectious agents.",
       "The artificial system of classification was given by Linnaeus — it was based on only a few morphological characters (e.g., number of stamens).",
       "The natural system of classification was given by Bentham and Hooker — based on natural affinities and similarity of many characters.",
       "The phylogenetic system was given by Engler and Prantl, and Hutchinson — based on evolutionary relationships among organisms.",
